\\(17 × 2 = 34\\) and then shift it left one place (multiply by 10), getting \\(340\\). Write this above the 51, offset to the left by one column.\n\n3. **Add the two partial results:**\n\n   \\(340 + 51 = 391\\).\n\n---\n\n### Quick Check\n\nYou can always double‑check by using a different grouping:  \n\\(17 \\times 23 = 23 \\times 17\\).  \nDoing the same steps with the numbers reversed gives the same result, confirming the calculation.\n\n---\n\nSo either method shows the same clean answer: **391**."}],"role":"assistant"}},"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"inputTokens":85,"outputTokens":678,"serverToolUsage":{},"totalTokens":763}}539 2785
